  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c1bff6658b6d4fe18488eccfca7256bb, type: 3}
  m_Name: ManualPage4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  pageIndex: 3
  pageTitle: Frame Numbers
  leftPageBody: 'Frame Numbers:

    Frame numbers (as seen in tools like Wireshark)
    are not part of the protocols themselves but are used by network analysis tools
    to label packets in the order they were captured. They help observers track and
    reference specific packets during inspection. Frame numbers are mainly used for
    simplicity''s sake. Frame numbers in a single stream should be increasing for
    every valid packet in the stream.'
  rightPageBody: 'NOTE: Frame Numbers should be increasing per stream. A stream for
    one protocol and a stream for another have two different counters. Make sure
    you pay attention to the current stream and frame number you are investigating.'
